# The local model in one command (README "Local model (Ollama)"):
#   docker compose --env-file local-llm.env up --build
# It turns on the local-llm profile (ollama, then a one-shot pull of the catalogued model) and
# enables the ollama provider next to demo, which stays the default provider. Every other
# setting keeps its docker-compose.yml default. To keep your own .env settings as well, pass it
# first: docker compose --env-file .env --env-file local-llm.env up --build
COMPOSE_PROFILES=local-llm
PROVIDERS_ENABLED=demo,ollama
